WEBVTT

00:01.370 --> 00:03.420
We're going to the Moon!

00:04.790 --> 00:09.480
I was sure I'd never be shocked anymore,
no matter what you said we were making...

00:09.480 --> 00:12.450
A proper trip to the Moon
in the stone world, huh?

00:13.290 --> 00:14.540
The Moon?!

00:14.540 --> 00:15.820
But how?!

00:17.260 --> 00:20.200
The same way the Kingdom of
Science has always done it.

00:20.200 --> 00:22.500
Patiently, one step at a time.

00:22.500 --> 00:24.590
Nothing about this is the same.

00:24.590 --> 00:26.800
Everything about this is
different from before.

00:26.800 --> 00:28.670
Especially in its scope and ambition.

00:29.970 --> 00:32.490
But now that we know 
the enemy is on the Moon,

00:32.490 --> 00:37.180
surely we should want more than 
to simply await our fate again.

00:38.800 --> 00:43.080
So now, in this new world, we are
to desire the stars in the sky!

00:43.080 --> 00:44.140
Shit...

00:44.450 --> 00:47.230
Science is seriously nuts!

00:48.810 --> 00:51.440
Building rockets happens
to be Senku's specialty.

00:51.650 --> 00:54.650
All right, what do we need, Senku?

00:56.190 --> 00:59.500
We're going all over the
world to find materials.

01:01.620 --> 01:06.400
It's the start of the New
World Moon Tour Project!

02:37.280 --> 02:42.010
<b>"Treasure Island"</b>

02:51.850 --> 02:52.600
There!

02:56.820 --> 02:59.820
The wretched petrification is
being undone before my eyes!

02:59.820 --> 03:01.190
How strange...

03:01.190 --> 03:02.240
Isn't it?!

03:02.240 --> 03:04.740
Awesome, right?

03:06.070 --> 03:06.870
Huh?

03:09.520 --> 03:12.580
Why are <i>you</i> being so smug about this, Ginro?

03:13.070 --> 03:14.750
It's all right.

03:14.750 --> 03:16.680
Everyone's safe now.

03:18.710 --> 03:20.810
I am awestruck.

03:20.810 --> 03:22.760
So this is the sorcery known as "science."

03:23.340 --> 03:27.930
If only we'd had this when the horrible
petrification devices rained down...

03:29.030 --> 03:33.060
Are there no more of those
petrification devices?

03:33.760 --> 03:36.420
The master ordered me to destroy all of them.

03:36.420 --> 03:38.730
Save for the one the bandits took.

03:39.730 --> 03:42.760
And that's that last one.

03:44.810 --> 03:47.530
We can revive anyone as long
as we have all their pieces.

03:47.860 --> 03:50.580
Let's wake everyone up and
get the hell out of here.

03:50.580 --> 03:51.400
Yeah!

03:51.400 --> 03:51.920
Indeed.

03:51.920 --> 03:53.080
Let's go!

03:53.950 --> 03:55.270
<i>Everyone...</i>

04:06.120 --> 04:09.680
<i>I'm sorry we couldn't bring you back, Dad.</i>

04:10.540 --> 04:11.870
<i>I'm about to...</i>

04:14.270 --> 04:16.330
We're waking up enemy soldiers, too?!

04:16.330 --> 04:17.310
Is that safe?!

04:18.540 --> 04:20.140
It shouldn't be a problem.

04:20.480 --> 04:24.620
They were simply deceived 
into serving the false Master.

04:24.620 --> 04:27.320
Ryusui-chan wants all the enemies, too.

04:27.320 --> 04:28.920
That's just how he is, you know?

04:45.290 --> 04:49.900
I was glad to learn that you were alive 
after twenty years, young master Soyuz.

04:50.560 --> 04:51.350
No...

04:52.030 --> 04:53.390
Master.

05:00.850 --> 05:03.650
I'm sad about Soyuz's dad.

05:04.010 --> 05:08.630
His body's right there,
but we can't even talk to him.

05:15.440 --> 05:20.460
Well, we've got one more important
mission before we head out.

05:20.460 --> 05:22.180
An important mission?

05:22.180 --> 05:23.550
What's that?

05:25.120 --> 05:30.100
We're making this island an
ally of the Kingdom of Science.

05:31.250 --> 05:32.850
What do you mean by that, Senku?

05:34.040 --> 05:38.680
Going to the Moon is going to
be a super massive project.

05:38.680 --> 05:40.830
There are some special 
crafts we're gonna have to

05:40.830 --> 05:42.730
build here on Treasure Island.

05:43.530 --> 05:49.620
We'll get all the islanders on our
side and have them help us out good.

05:50.570 --> 05:52.330
H-Help?

05:52.330 --> 05:58.040
I-I just saw the really devious
face Senku sometimes makes.

05:58.320 --> 06:01.310
We're going to need an unprecedented
amount of manpower.

06:01.310 --> 06:03.920
That's a requirement we can't work around.

06:04.570 --> 06:07.150
I hope it works out as well as you think.

06:07.150 --> 06:09.800
Being a ruler isn't all that easy.

06:12.450 --> 06:17.940
The islanders were just freed from
the shackles of the man named Ibara.

06:18.350 --> 06:22.060
Not all of them are as industrious as Kinro.

06:23.730 --> 06:25.420
We aren't ruling over anyone.

06:25.420 --> 06:27.290
We're having the islanders
choose for themselves

06:27.290 --> 06:30.390
to become allies of the Kingdom of Science.

06:30.390 --> 06:33.740
"Choosing for themselves"
being the important part.

06:33.740 --> 06:35.950
Right, mentalist?

06:36.940 --> 06:40.960
Senku-chan's starting to get how it works.

06:42.450 --> 06:44.750
I-I want to take care of it.

06:46.150 --> 06:50.090
Dad worked to unify this
island and everyone on it.

06:50.970 --> 06:53.050
I have to continue his work.

06:56.800 --> 06:58.100
All right.

06:58.100 --> 07:00.580
I'm leaving this all to you, then.

07:00.580 --> 07:01.770
R-Right.

07:02.820 --> 07:04.270
What's this?

07:05.380 --> 07:06.650
Lemme see!

07:06.650 --> 07:08.520
What are we making?

07:15.770 --> 07:17.120
Guys!

07:18.910 --> 07:22.120
We have to make a really big facility quick.

07:22.120 --> 07:23.730
We need some help!

07:25.510 --> 07:28.970
I want everyone to help,
for the sake of the island!

07:59.020 --> 08:00.000
Yeah!

08:00.000 --> 08:01.080
Damn!

08:01.080 --> 08:02.750
Look at that giant thing go!

08:04.890 --> 08:06.710
Wait, where's Senku?

08:15.470 --> 08:17.550
A-ha.

08:18.780 --> 08:22.060
Yo, Senku, what the hell are
you doing all by yourself?

08:24.990 --> 08:28.060
Working on a hella exhilarating craft.

08:28.060 --> 08:29.070
Oh, shit!

08:35.850 --> 08:37.000
What's this stuff?

08:37.840 --> 08:39.540
It's called zeolite.

08:39.540 --> 08:41.460
It's like a desiccant.

08:42.290 --> 08:45.130
That's why you were all crusty.

08:46.800 --> 08:50.960
Gunpowder and salt and... iron?

08:50.960 --> 08:53.440
Hey, Senku, what's that?

08:54.350 --> 08:56.860
My dear Chrome-sama's badass sorcery.

08:57.350 --> 08:59.020
The flame test reaction.

09:00.930 --> 09:03.390
Check out my badass sorcery!

09:03.700 --> 09:05.890
Rainbow Bridge!

09:10.920 --> 09:11.650
But...

09:12.260 --> 09:14.660
What exactly are you doing with all this?

09:15.910 --> 09:19.530
You could say it's just a little more
persuasion in case the islanders need any.

09:19.530 --> 09:20.740
Oh, shit!

09:20.740 --> 09:23.290
I mean, I've done it before, but...

09:21.930 --> 09:23.290
Mm-hm.

09:23.640 --> 09:25.750
I see.

09:27.430 --> 09:30.370
Why don't I <i>really</i> hype it up for them, then?

09:31.090 --> 09:31.850
Apologies.

09:32.300 --> 09:34.800
I shall begin preparations for our guests.

09:36.050 --> 09:37.990
I haven't said anything.

09:37.990 --> 09:41.050
That one's crazy good at anticipating things.

09:42.180 --> 09:44.130
What's about to happen?

09:49.450 --> 09:54.070
All right, let's go ahead with the test!

09:54.070 --> 09:55.240
Yup.

10:01.310 --> 10:03.160
It's working.

10:03.610 --> 10:04.970
You can try talking to them.

10:06.040 --> 10:07.750
T-Testing.

10:08.230 --> 10:09.320
Testing.

10:09.760 --> 10:10.750
We're...

10:10.750 --> 10:12.370
<i>on the water.</i>

10:12.370 --> 10:13.920
Yes!

10:13.920 --> 10:16.110
W-We hear you, Kirisame.

10:16.420 --> 10:17.510
Can you hear me?

10:17.510 --> 10:20.640
Yes, I hear you, Soyuz-sama.

10:20.970 --> 10:23.470
<i>It's like we're speaking close by.</i>

10:24.340 --> 10:24.970
Wow!

10:25.300 --> 10:26.630
This is science?!

10:26.630 --> 10:27.330
I'm amazed!

10:27.330 --> 10:29.050
Science is awesome!

10:40.780 --> 10:43.410
<b>Cotton Candy</b>

10:40.780 --> 10:43.410
It's sweet and fluffy!

10:43.410 --> 10:46.410
Here you are! Firm noodles,
rich soup, and extra green onions.

10:47.810 --> 10:53.750
Blue-spotted wrasse poêlé with water
celery and cauliflower fungus sautee.

10:49.620 --> 10:55.130
<b>Francois</b>

10:56.250 --> 10:57.680
The scent...

11:00.640 --> 11:02.390
It's sho good!

11:03.250 --> 11:05.650
What is this? I can see really clearly!

11:05.650 --> 11:06.700
Really?

11:21.820 --> 11:23.530
What's going on here?

11:24.410 --> 11:25.740
All ready!

11:25.740 --> 11:27.410
I gathered everyone here!

11:29.210 --> 11:32.210
Damn it, Gen, you were 
eavesdropping, weren't you?

11:38.690 --> 11:40.800
Senku, do you have a minute?

11:42.230 --> 11:46.960
I-I'm planning to stay on this island.

11:47.350 --> 11:48.890
To help us start over again.

11:49.490 --> 11:51.030
And to help it develop.

11:52.490 --> 11:53.740
Yeah.

11:53.740 --> 11:55.860
If that's what you want, go for it.

11:58.180 --> 12:00.610
Senku... Thanks.

12:01.840 --> 12:04.740
Why are you thanking me? Dumbass.

12:04.740 --> 12:09.120
The goal of all our missions is to solve
the mystery of humanity's petrification.

12:11.050 --> 12:13.070
Yeah. You're right.

12:13.900 --> 12:16.540
So all of you can set out.

12:17.360 --> 12:19.530
I still remember how to 
make the revival fluid, too.

12:19.530 --> 12:21.800
You remember all that after only one time?

12:21.800 --> 12:23.850
Your memory is insane.

12:23.850 --> 12:29.260
It'll take a while, but I promise
I'll revive all the villagers,

12:30.530 --> 12:32.230
as the island's Master.

12:33.480 --> 12:35.550
We'll help, as well.

12:35.550 --> 12:38.120
Allow us, Master Soyuz.

12:38.120 --> 12:40.690
We're fighting against the
so-called Why-Man, are we not?

12:40.950 --> 12:41.880
That's right.

12:41.880 --> 12:45.450
Which is why I want you two to go with Senku.

12:46.700 --> 12:50.810
We'll have to travel the world and revive 
all sorts of people to gather materials.

12:51.220 --> 12:53.710
They're going to need some strong warriors.

12:59.070 --> 13:00.610
Understood.

13:00.610 --> 13:03.130
I vow to prove myself useful.

13:05.200 --> 13:06.980
I know, right?!

13:06.980 --> 13:09.270
So come on, Matsukaze-kun!

13:09.270 --> 13:12.370
You should follow your master's
reincarnation-ish person

13:12.370 --> 13:16.080
and become my stude—I mean, guard!

13:16.080 --> 13:16.800
Yes, sir!

13:16.800 --> 13:19.060
I shall prove myself useful.

13:19.060 --> 13:22.970
Soyuz and Ginro are saying
the same thing, but...

13:22.970 --> 13:25.290
One's saying it for the sake of
everyone, the other for his own...

13:25.290 --> 13:27.570
Really shows a difference in character.

13:28.780 --> 13:31.510
Matsukaze's skill is something
even I would want.

13:31.510 --> 13:33.350
It's not a bad thing.

13:33.350 --> 13:37.710
He doesn't have the same kind of honest
greed that you do, Ryusui-chan.

13:37.710 --> 13:40.540
He's leveled up his carried-away-ness.

13:37.830 --> 13:40.540
Carried Away
Level 2

13:42.310 --> 13:43.120
What the?!

13:43.120 --> 13:44.460
It just got dark all of a sudden...

13:44.460 --> 13:46.470
<i>Do you hear me, all?</i>

13:47.180 --> 13:49.100
<i>We're gonna show you something that's</i>

13:49.100 --> 13:53.100
<i>going to leave the whole of Treasure
Island speechless and wanting more!</i>

13:53.100 --> 13:56.600
Rainbow Bridge Max Level!

13:56.850 --> 13:58.310
Aye!

13:58.310 --> 14:00.060
Here we go!

14:26.300 --> 14:27.890
Whoa!

14:29.850 --> 14:33.020
I never thought I'd see fireworks again.

14:35.120 --> 14:36.530
Fireworks...

14:37.180 --> 14:40.720
Back in our era, they were meant to quell

14:40.720 --> 14:46.030
the spirits of the deceased 
and send them off.

14:47.610 --> 14:53.830
I think Senku-chan wanted you
to see this, on this island.

15:21.480 --> 15:23.560
Look! There's another one!

15:26.360 --> 15:27.600
See that, Senku?

15:27.600 --> 15:30.150
That one was a smiley face, wasn't it?

15:30.400 --> 15:34.100
Yeah, I guess that was about
130 meters in diameter.

15:34.100 --> 15:35.990
That makes it a Number Four firework.

15:35.990 --> 15:41.200
Sodium oxalate for the yellow, and maybe
some strontium nitrate for the red...

15:41.200 --> 15:44.430
What kind of preschooler
says <i>that</i> about fireworks?

15:44.430 --> 15:47.860
And you're way too giddy
for a grown-up, Byakuya.

15:47.860 --> 15:50.100
You're making ten billion times
as big a fuss as I am.

15:52.080 --> 15:54.630
I've always loved fireworks.

15:55.350 --> 16:01.140
The craftspeople who make fireworks
did a lot of prep for today.

16:03.100 --> 16:07.440
And just for an instant, 
it dazzles everyone from above.

16:10.190 --> 16:15.950
The science of gunpowder
lives on in the hearts of many

16:16.580 --> 16:19.740
and gives hope for the future.

16:48.250 --> 16:50.070
Why are you here?

16:50.070 --> 16:52.560
Just an early morning stroll.

16:52.560 --> 16:55.000
Is it not the same for you?

16:58.090 --> 17:03.500
Thousands of years ago,
Byakuya and the other astronauts

17:04.290 --> 17:10.550
set foot here for the first time
in an utterly deserted new world.

17:13.230 --> 17:19.220
Though they've long since turned to dirt,
aside from a few fragments of rock.

17:22.000 --> 17:24.140
That's not true!

17:30.120 --> 17:35.070
You, I, and everyone else will 
someday die and return to dust.

17:35.670 --> 17:42.660
But their will is passed down, refined,
and carried on into the future.

17:45.210 --> 17:47.900
Isn't that what humanity calls "science"?

17:48.330 --> 17:51.630
That's what you taught me, Senku.

17:53.850 --> 17:55.380
Yeah, that's right.

17:55.880 --> 17:59.220
We're going way farther than
those goofy astronauts.

17:59.220 --> 18:00.790
We're going to the Moon.

18:03.330 --> 18:07.630
It's not true that Byakuya and
his team left nothing behind.

18:08.110 --> 18:10.810
In fact, they connected everything for us.

18:17.020 --> 18:20.910
This island turned out to be 
a literal treasure island!

18:26.790 --> 18:29.040
Bye-bye!

18:30.640 --> 18:33.510
We've got the power of radio on our side.

18:33.510 --> 18:35.610
This isn't goodbye forever.

18:35.610 --> 18:37.430
Spare us your tears.

18:38.220 --> 18:40.650
No matter how ridiculously
far apart we are,

18:41.320 --> 18:44.200
we're connected bye a wave of science.

18:46.170 --> 18:51.210
This island is the Kingdom
of Science's powerful ally.

18:55.670 --> 18:57.850
Senku... Until we meet again.

19:00.440 --> 19:01.760
So...

19:02.140 --> 19:04.990
Now that we've acquired
platinum from Treasure Island,

19:04.990 --> 19:07.200
we'll be pumping out a 
crap-ton of revival fluid.

19:07.200 --> 19:10.250
We're going all over the world
to gather people and resources.

19:10.250 --> 19:11.360
I want it!

19:11.360 --> 19:13.390
And the Kingdom of Science will make it!

19:13.390 --> 19:15.550
A luxury Moon tour passenger ship!

19:15.550 --> 19:18.160
A beautiful ship of the stars!

19:19.730 --> 19:22.460
I've made some ships in my time,

19:22.460 --> 19:25.250
but I can't even imagine what
this one will look like!

19:25.250 --> 19:27.630
Is it big? Is it small?

19:27.630 --> 19:29.780
Is it like a balloon?

19:29.780 --> 19:31.600
That's about the right size, at least.

19:32.350 --> 19:35.900
The Soyuz spaceship Byakuya-san
was on was a three-seater.

19:35.900 --> 19:38.440
So we aren't taking more
than a few people, huh?

19:38.440 --> 19:39.720
Who will be going?

19:40.050 --> 19:42.020
We'll need a pilot.

19:42.020 --> 19:43.030
That's me!

19:43.030 --> 19:45.990
And without a science user on
board, there's no point in going.

19:45.990 --> 19:49.700
It'll have to be whoever is the
most apt when the rocket's done.

19:49.700 --> 19:51.070
<i>It's Senku.</i>

19:51.070 --> 19:52.330
<i>Yeah, it's definitely Senku.</i>

19:52.330 --> 19:53.680
<i>Senku for sure.</i>

19:54.560 --> 19:58.300
That's so like you not to
be certain of that, even.

19:58.880 --> 20:01.020
And I guess we'll need a fighting force.

20:01.020 --> 20:02.810
We'll want people we can mobilize.

20:03.450 --> 20:06.400
I'd rather not think about
combat on the Moon...

20:06.400 --> 20:08.680
But we don't even know what Why-Man is.

20:10.220 --> 20:13.410
So we'll need the strongest we have!

20:13.410 --> 20:15.250
That makes things simple.

20:15.250 --> 20:16.410
How do we choose?

20:16.410 --> 20:18.070
Another official duel?

20:18.310 --> 20:22.280
We aren't going to need another
tournament just for that.

20:23.200 --> 20:26.040
We already have our strongest.

20:41.190 --> 20:42.520
They're back!

20:46.360 --> 20:48.150
Welcome back!

20:50.450 --> 20:51.990
Ruri-chan!

20:51.990 --> 20:53.050
Look at us!

20:53.050 --> 20:58.530
I and the adventure team brought
back some awesome treasures!

20:57.940 --> 21:10.950
Carried Away
Level 3

20:59.960 --> 21:04.330
And why are you getting all carried
away, acting like the chief?

21:04.330 --> 21:09.010
I guess because he's gotten the super
powerful Matsukaze-chan on his side...

21:09.010 --> 21:10.200
By dumb luck.

21:15.980 --> 21:17.040
Huh?

21:17.790 --> 21:20.170
They've all lost their cracks!

21:21.000 --> 21:21.920
Right?

21:22.250 --> 21:24.280
Could that mean...

21:24.280 --> 21:25.450
That's right!

21:27.030 --> 21:30.100
It's the petrification device and an
infinite supply of rejuvenation fluid!

21:30.100 --> 21:33.850
Petrify someone and revive them,
and you heal any injury, no matter how bad!

21:33.850 --> 21:36.230
It's the Dr. Stone set!

21:38.630 --> 21:41.940
Science truly is mighty.

21:43.380 --> 21:48.030
It's the terrible calamity that
turned everyone to stone...

21:48.290 --> 21:52.570
And now, we're making even that work for us.

21:54.770 --> 21:56.350
Does that mean...

21:57.600 --> 21:59.930
Finally... He'll finally...

22:02.160 --> 22:03.370
Yeah.

22:03.760 --> 22:06.840
Let's get him out of cold sleep.

22:07.860 --> 22:11.040
The strongest high school primate...

22:11.040 --> 22:13.490
Shishio Tsukasa!

23:52.070 --> 23:55.030
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:55.030 --> 24:00.040
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants,
animals, and production methods described are based on reality.
Foraging and making things on your own accord is extremely dangerous
and, in some cases, illegal. Please do not imitate without expertise.</b>
